{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e","id":1329900,"title":"Atlantean Pantheon in 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-08T08:51:33-07:00","id":1329900,"title":"Atlantean Pantheon in 2E","content":"<b>Notice:</b> No need for voicing dislikes over this Pantheon - this topic is about using it in games. Don't like Atlanteans - just move away from here.<br /> <br /> Topic about how to use Atlantean Pantheon that will have premiere for 2E in <b>Scion Companion: Mysteries of the World</b>. We have <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-teros-of-atlantis-scion-companion/\" target=\"_blank\">first preview on it in blog post about creating your own Pantheons</a>.<br /> <br /> I'm great fan of pulp and <b>Mage: The Awakening</b> - and wanting to use Atlanteans in my game. <b>I think about making it 'first Pantheon of the World' - where rest of live Pantheons sprung from.</b> Could it be run like this in Scion 2E, without large clashes with rest of setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T09:04:24-07:00","id":1329904,"title":"","content":"When first hearing of Atlantis in Scion, my brain picked on the idea of the island being something known for a long time but not considered that special.<br /> <br /> Essentially it is a normal island in the middle of the Atlantic. Its single strange feature is a very tall featureless spire in the exact middle of the island but it hasnt done anything for the past several centuries. So while it is mysterious, lack of any development or any possibility of interaction made it so that most people assumes its unsolvable.<br /> In modern days estate development have acquired the island and multiple resort hotels have been built on the island and there is a very kitsch &quot;atlantis for tourist&quot; culture there.<br /> <br /> Im still not sure if ill use it in a game but i really like the concept. Maybe pre-visitation scions there on vacation or something. Ill figure something out eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T11:45:53-07:00","id":1329944,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Teros, but I wouldn't be the one to say they were the first religion. Certainly not definitively. I mean, they say that Atlantis was the first city, but the Deva say that this World is but the latest cycle and it'll go through even more of them. The Theoi claim this is the Fifth age, after the Reign of Kronos. Most Pantheons have their own stories about how they shaped the World from nothing, and you know what? They're all right.<br /> <br /> So... Having the Atlantis Gods in Scion? Great. I probably will.<br /> <br /> Trying to say they're better than the other Pantheons in any definitive way is really missing the point of the gameline.<br /> <br /> As for running the Teros in your game, I think the Companion will have some advise. That Atlantis is an island that long ago used its miracle technology to fold space in on itself, vanishing the island from the World at large. It exists, but isolated, and stagnant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T11:59:32-07:00","id":1329949,"title":"","content":"Atlantis is an Ancient city. They fight the Wraiths of the past, abandoned by the population...<br /> And Jason Momoa is there, as a king or as a warrior, not sure...<br /> <br /> I liked a lot the Atlantean pantheon and purview from 1e, actually I had a plan to use it as an old adversary of the Netjer (in a way similar to Vanir and Aesir) that eventually vanished when Atlantis was destroyed by the water Titan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T13:41:13-07:00","id":1329962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1329949#post1329949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atlantis is an Ancient city. They fight the Wraiths of the past, abandoned by the population...<br /> And Jason Momoa is there, as a king or as a warrior, not sure...</div> </div> </div> </div>With Kevin Sorbo as his aging father or mentor (for those old enough to remember <i>that</i> movie...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T18:42:18-07:00","id":1330009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1329962#post1329962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Kevin Sorbo as his aging father or mentor (for those old enough to remember <i>that</i> movie...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t get off topic, he is from another pantheon... but I think you are right, there is something about Atlantis... \ud83d\ude02","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T06:19:55-07:00","id":1330235,"title":"","content":"Rift off Mage the Awakening and have Atlantis scattered. Many different places in the World are shadows and remnants of Atlantis. Many different peoples carry the true blood of Atlantis. The Gods of Atlantis are neither living nor dead but exist as scraps of story and distored shadows in pop culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T11:45:26-07:00","id":1330283,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m inclined not use the Atlantan Pantheon for the World, though they do sound really cool from what we\u2019ve heard. My inclination for the World is to make the submerged ruins of Atlantis Theoi Terra-Incognita where Poseidon holds his personal court away from Olympus.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t come up with what if anything i\u2019m going to do with the Teros, but I have a seed of an idea that might involve the Masks of the Mythos mechanics as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T12:15:46-07:00","id":1330284,"title":"","content":"I don't own Scion 2e but i own all 1e and if they bring back Atlantis in a book I know I'll buy tgat book which means I will but the core books. <br /> <br /> Also having the First Deities of Atlantis being Time and Space is BRILLIANT! So much greatness. Same with the idea of a hidden space folding island city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T15:24:41-07:00","id":1330305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1330009#post1330009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don\u2019t get off topic, he is from another pantheon... but I think you are right, there is something about Atlantis... \ud83d\ude02</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kull_the_Conqueror\" target=\"_blank\">that movie</a> he was in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T19:05:08-07:00","id":1333202,"title":"","content":"As a question from someone who doesn't follow Scion 2e news do we have any active information on the Atlantis pantheon. Now, I do know they don't give dates for book releases but do know what book its in and where said book is on the spectrum of being written and stuff? <br /> <br /> Additionally, do we have any fan made or mini-official versions of the Atlantis pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T19:52:26-07:00","id":1333207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1333202#post1333202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a question from someone who doesn't follow Scion 2e news do we have any active information on the Atlantis pantheon. Now, I do know they don't give dates for book releases but do know what book its in and where said book is on the spectrum of being written and stuff? <br /> <br /> Additionally, do we have any fan made or mini-official versions of the Atlantis pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>The blog post at the top of the thread was our last in depth update, but their Virtues have been mentioned (Nostalgia and Vision), and the general aesthetic of their pantheon motif/PSP which is Clarke\u2019s Law sufficiently advanced technology with crystal-tech, laser harmonics, nanites, etc to perform their miracles.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re very intentionally a Jack Kirby Homage with Atlantis itself evoking Wakanda, and their deities being cosmic \u201cNew Gods\u201d style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-29-2019, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T19:56:44-07:00","id":1333210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1333207#post1333207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The blog post at the top of the thread was our last in depth update, but their Virtues have been mentioned (Nostalgia and Vision), and the general aesthetic of their pantheon motif/PSP which is Clarke\u2019s Law sufficiently advanced technology with crystal-tech, laser harmonics, nanites, etc to perform their miracles.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re very intentionally a Jack Kirby Homage with Atlantis itself evoking Wakanda, and their deities being cosmic \u201cNew Gods\u201d style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh lord, I think I am in love. That sounds PERFECT and awesome and I want. I want. I want. To the point that even though I don't own Scion 2e I will buy said book and then probably will go out and buy Scion 2e almost immediately afterward just to be able to use Atlantis stuff. <br /> <br /> This stuff is brilliant. Thanks for telling me what we know. I appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T22:38:18-07:00","id":1333221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1333210#post1333210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh lord, I think I am in love. That sounds PERFECT and awesome and I want. I want. I want. To the point that even though I don't own Scion 2e I will buy said book and then probably will go out and buy Scion 2e almost immediately afterward just to be able to use Atlantis stuff.<br /> <br /> This stuff is brilliant. Thanks for telling me what we know. I appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess I want to use it for Adventure! as well as Scion, but I also know I'm going to write a crossover between Trinity and Scion at one point, so that might count for less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T23:22:36-07:00","id":1333224,"title":"","content":"Other things I know from Tidbits gathered for the 2e Atlantis Pantheon<br /> <br /> Pantheon: The Teros<br /> Pantheon Virtues: Nostalgia vs Vision<br /> Pantheon Motif: <i>Sufficiently Advanced Technology is Indistinguishable From a Miracle</i><br /> Pantheon Signature Purview: Demiurgy<br /> Boons Names<ul><li>God-Sight</li> <li>Hypertech Upgrade</li> </ul><br /> Alas, we don't know what the mechanics of Demiurgy and its Boons are... Nor do we know the Asset Skills for the Teros Pantheon Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T11:54:45-07:00","id":1333287,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> yeah, the idea of using the idea of Scion Atlantis in a Trinity Continuum game is strong with me as well. hehe<br /> <br /> Depending on how things work for them I could see finding ways to take their powers and bring them to Trinity. If not then simly use the fluff and descriptions while having Atlantean heroes being either Inspired or full on Novas or Psiads. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1333224#post1333224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other things I know from Tidbits gathered for the 2e Atlantis Pantheon<br /> <br /> Pantheon: The Teros<br /> Pantheon Virtues: Nostalgia vs Vision<br /> Pantheon Motif: <i>Sufficiently Advanced Technology is Indistinguishable From a Miracle</i><br /> Pantheon Signature Purview: Demiurgy<br /> Boons Names<ul><li>God-Sight</li> <li>Hypertech Upgrade</li> </ul><br /> Alas, we don't know what the mechanics of Demiurgy and its Boons are... Nor do we know the Asset Skills for the Teros Pantheon Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy oh boy this sounds even more amazing. I want, I want. Soo cool. I hope they give us more info and such. Even without full details knowing that this is being developed, and maybe where it is being developed for, would be useful. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I want. I really like Atlantis. I liked it a lot in Scion 1e Demigod. I also liked its mention in Mage. So I want more.<br /> <br /> I want a secretly playable cool Atlantis. That or I want an Atlantis that while Fallen has just enough potential that players could bring it back, even in a hidden state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T13:11:16-07:00","id":1333293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1333287#post1333287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh boy oh boy this sounds even more amazing. I want, I want. Soo cool. I hope they give us more info and such. Even without full details knowing that this is being developed, and maybe where it is being developed for, would be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>2E Scion Companion, as mentioned in the OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T13:53:33-07:00","id":1333296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1333293#post1333293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2E Scion Companion, as mentioned in the OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slap's forehead. I seriously blanked out on 'Scion Companion' and thought it was Mysteries of the World as the title and so when my attempt to look that up found nothing I was like &quot;well, I guess things changed&quot;. lol <br /> <br /> But yeah, okay, lol, it being in Scion Companion makes lots of sense. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T15:29:55-07:00","id":1333311,"title":"","content":"I'm glad to see I'm not the only one thinking of using this version of Atlantis with Adventure! or Mage.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Given that one of their virtues is Nostalgia, is it wrong of me to want to try to make Member Berries an Atlantian relic?\ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T15:39:46-07:00","id":1333313,"title":"","content":"The Scion Companion will have the title of &quot;Mysteries of the World&quot;, thus the confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T17:01:00-07:00","id":1333324,"title":"","content":"I have always loved Atlantis! I love the 1e focus in Mage better than 2e just touching on it. I am considering weaving Atlantis into the creation history of Exalted 3E making it the the basis for Exalted / CoD / Mage / Scion. <br /> <br /> First city at the center of creation with the Exalted universe bubbled inside the others. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"