k you, Meghan)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T16:20:00-07:00","id":1334260,"title":"","content":"Many years ago I ran the WoD fan supplement for Highlander with them being the blood of Atlantis, very cool. Using the Highlander with Atlantis influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T13:26:09-07:00","id":1338174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1333900#post1333900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another tidbit for you: their Asset Skills are Science and Technology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Science and Technology, you say? Hmmm, it will be interesting to put Theros and Atlantis as first Pantheon to <i><b>scientificlly</b></i> researching other Pantheons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like - from Crystal Dynamics <b>Tomb Raider</b> series - 'Helheim of Norse is in reality Avalon of Tuatha De Danann' kind of pulp. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T13:56:15-07:00","id":1338178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1338174#post1338174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Science and Technology, you say? Hmmm, it will be interesting to put Theros and Atlantis as first Pantheon to <i><b>scientificlly</b></i> researching other Pantheons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like - from Crystal Dynamics <b>Tomb Raider</b> series - 'Helheim of Norse is in reality Avalon of Tuatha De Danann' kind of pulp. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>... Please don't imply that the other Pantheons and Cultures have no idea how science and technology worked. :/ Probably not your intention but a bit of that came off.<br /> <br /> Also, Avalon has precisely nothing to do with the Tuatha de. That's Arthurian, which is a pop mix of Welsh and Saxon mixed with later fanfiction of French and more modern English origin. Scion is written with the assumption that Avalon is Avalon, and Helheim is Helheim, and no the two aren't the same thing, nor are either of them Tir na nOg, or the Lost Four Cities of the Tuatha. Why would you want to take these several distinctive and emphatically <b>different</b> locations and rob them of their flavor by saying &quot;Also these are all the same!&quot;?<br /> <br /> Now to keep it vaguely on topic, Atlantis, I managed to dig up one more tidbit... And this'll probably be the last we get until the Companion is released.<br /> <br /> <b>The Scent of the Divine for the Teros</b>: The smell of ozone, the sound of crashing waves, and the inescapable feeling that nothing is as it should be","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-27-2019, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T15:00:50-07:00","id":1338190,"title":"","content":"To be honest, back in 1E, I was fascinated by the Atlantean Pantheon as being their own actual Pantheon rather than just a renaming of the Greek Gods in a similar fashion as Rome did. That they were given a unique culture (even if there were a lot of gaps in the fine details) rather than just a copy of Greek culture that has been done so many times previously was intriguing to me. Then came the Titan corruption of Atlantis and how it was the Scions of the Atlantean Gods that seemed to have been turned against them, transforming Atlantean culture into a dark reflection of what it was... and how the other Pantheons had to band against this transformed Atlantis to save the World. Yet even with this tragedy, some of the pettiness of the Gods from other Pantheons showed through on how they felt the need to not only stop the corrupted Atlantis, but to completely erase all traces of it, down to every last member of the culture (presumably even those who may have escaped its corruption) because they felt they couldn't risk the chance that anyone got away to undo what they had done. Over all... the story that was woven about Atlantis... its rise, corruption and eventual fall was as epic as it was ultimately tragic in my eyes... and gave me inspiration for me to work on a plot line of its eventual redemption (what can I say... I love stories of redemption, even if they end tragically).<br /> <br /> So I began scouring the information provided, looking for some plausible means to potentially bring this pantheon back for my own stories and games. It was made clear that any Scion of Atlantis would be different than those normally found in the game, since the Gods of Atlantis were presumably destroyed by the Titans (or at least imprisoned by their corrupted Scions and weakened by thousands of years of not receiving any worship). Then, in the adventure that was provided about Atlantis, I saw what I needed... the ship that had sunk and crashed into a submerged Atlantean Temple was what I would use to allow the Atlantean Gods to escape their imprisonment by their Titan corrupted children and gave them the chance they would need to redeem their Pantheon.<br /> <br /> To put it simply, the basis for the Campaign, the Atlantean Gods would use the last of their power to infuse their essence into mortals to be reborn as the last generation of Atlantean Scions (basically become what in 2E is Incarnate Scions). Part of this required tracking down the last traces of Atlantean bloodlines with in the world (even the combined might of all the Pantheons couldn't completely wipe out all traces of Atlantis, as some had escaped to other cultures before the corruption of Atlantis and had remained hidden within those cultures). This scattered the would be Scions initially, so as to escape initial notice of both the Titans and the Gods that still sought to keep Atlantis from rising (and potentially dooming the world again). These reborn Atlantean Gods would have to find each other, reclaim their lost birthright and avoid their enemies to regain the power they once had... starting off as Heroes. Not only would the Titans be after them (to corrupt the essence of the Gods they couldn't before), but also the other Pantheons too (or rather their Scions tasked with making sure that Atlantis remained but a forgotten memory). It was going to be an epic game, where the players would be tempted by power, hunted for crimes their ancestors had committed and have to choose whether to remain true to the Gods they had been or become something different (while they may have the essence of the Atlantean Gods within them, they were not those Gods themselves, but new incarnations, free to choose their own path, for good or ill).<br /> <br /> To be honest, once the Pantheon is reintroduced to Scion 2E in Mysteries of the World, I may try to adapt this idea to what is presented... as it was an amazing story that I would still like to continue with (never did get past the Hero portion of the original game). Regardless, I am looking forward to seeing what Mysteries of the World contains... especially in regards to Atlantis. I know it wasn't the favorite of many fans of 1E (though I think the hate was more from a very vocal few than any sentiment shaded by the majority of fans), but it was one that gave me a huge amount of inspiration. I hope that it will do so again in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T11:52:10-07:00","id":1338325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1338178#post1338178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Please don't imply that the other Pantheons and Cultures have no idea how science and technology worked. :/ Probably not your intention but a bit of that came off.<br /> <br /> Also, Avalon has precisely nothing to do with the Tuatha de. That's Arthurian, which is a pop mix of Welsh and Saxon mixed with later fanfiction of French and more modern English origin. Scion is written with the assumption that Avalon is Avalon, and Helheim is Helheim, and no the two aren't the same thing, nor are either of them Tir na nOg, or the Lost Four Cities of the Tuatha. Why would you want to take these several distinctive and emphatically <b>different</b> locations and rob them of their flavor by saying &quot;Also these are all the same!&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <br /> Umm not to be confrontational, but they weren't saying any of that at all. They said the first to scientifically research the other Patheons and how the divine works scientifically. Which is not at all the same as saying the only ones to use science or technology, I really have no idea how you jumped to that conclusion. Same with the Helheim and Avalon mention, it wasn't even a mention to Scion. Like they said, which I think you missed, they were talking about maybe being like one of the Tomb Raider games where Avalon was actually also known as Helheim. Again, not at all saying that about Scion. <br /> I know you meant well, but please read a comment before getting upset and making assumptions like that. <br /> I personally am really looking forward to seeing if this Atlantean Pantheon Purview will have the same draw as 1E Scire. I adored Scire. By far my favorite of the Pantheon Purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T06:42:11-07:00","id":1338614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1338190#post1338190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Shadowstripe whole chronicle idea)</div> </div> </div> </div>I so stole this whole chronicle idea - as <b>Mage: The Awakening</b> fan I already look for ways to make <i><b>Tomb Raider</b></i>-like game with <b>Scion</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T10:03:46-07:00","id":1339209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1338614#post1338614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I so stole this whole chronicle idea - as <b>Mage: The Awakening</b> fan I already look for ways to make <i><b>Tomb Raider</b></i>-like game with <b>Scion</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see this as a complement as to how epic the idea was. To be honest, I am thinking of reviving it in 2E when we get more information on the Atlantean Pantheon (hopefully including how it has been adapted to the very different world that 2E is compared to 1E).<br /> <br /> There was just something about the idea of Forgotten Gods being reborn into a world where those who had once been allies were now enemies and hunting them for crimes their descendants committed and were punished for in ages past. Of trying to reclaim an ancient birthright without letting it change the person you have since become into something you can't even remember being... all the while being persecuted for something you didn't do... and wondering why those ancient allies never came to your aid when you needed it and help stop things before they got out of hand. So many questions to ask... so few answers to find. What greater epic could there be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T15:45:21-07:00","id":1339455,"title":"","content":"The idea of being modern inheritors of an ancient past is brilliant to me. As is the questions you asked and the options that can be given in answer. Honestly, so much can be done with this at all levels of campaign. <br /> <br /> The idea of adventuring to bring back the fallen is quite fun because at any point it can transition into ruling the once fallen and fighting those who would be allies but became enemies while also making allies of those who might once have been enemies. <br /> <br /> I really hope we get material on the history and geography of the once Atlantean people. It would be a nice starting point towards making one's own campaign. <br /> <br /> Oh, as a note, I have to say I really like how the Atlantean Pantheon have their own set of gods rather than using standard Greek and such gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T16:50:44-07:00","id":1339468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1339455#post1339455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, as a note, I have to say I really like how the Atlantean Pantheon have their own set of gods rather than using standard Greek and such gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>This take doesn't even make sense, because when the allegory of Atlantis was first proposed as an example it was meant to be in opposition of an idealized older Greek culture, who were at war with Greece. They wouldn't have had a lot of overlap at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T18:17:52-07:00","id":1339487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1339468#post1339468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This take doesn't even make sense, because when the allegory of Atlantis was first proposed as an example it was meant to be in opposition of an idealized older Greek culture, who were at war with Greece. They wouldn't have had a lot of overlap at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nod. Yeah I know, but a lot of Atlantis myths and rpgs have them just using Greek Gods. So I am glad they don't here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T19:11:02-07:00","id":1339497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1339468#post1339468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This take doesn't even make sense, because when the allegory of Atlantis was first proposed as an example it was meant to be in opposition of an idealized older Greek culture, who were at war with Greece. They wouldn't have had a lot of overlap at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a Greek story (not really a myth as Plato didn\u2019t mean it to be taken literally - but that\u2019s splitting hairs here), and as far as they were concerned, any other gods were just other faces of their gods, and the kings of Atlantis (literally named for Atlas) were descended from Poseidon. It would make perfect sense as Theoi Terra Incognita.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T20:58:33-07:00","id":1339518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1339497#post1339497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would make perfect sense as Theoi Terra Incognita.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Terra Incognita that Atlanteans and Theoi fighted over. \ud83d\ude0e Same can be made for Troy and other mythical cities! \u2764\ufe0f<br /> <br /> As I plan to let players choose other Panteons Patrons and later uncover their true heritage as Athlanteans Scions - What could be good common grounds for Atlanteans and other Pantheons? Like, what can have Atlanteans and Asir in common?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-05-2019, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:57:35-07:00","id":1339707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1339497#post1339497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s a Greek story (not really a myth as Plato didn\u2019t mean it to be taken literally - but that\u2019s splitting hairs here), and as far as they were concerned, any other gods were just other faces of their gods, and the kings of Atlantis (literally named for Atlas) were descended from Poseidon. It would make perfect sense as Theoi Terra Incognita.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would make an interesting game scenario where a group of Theoi scions and a group of Atlantean scions come into conflict over said Terra Incognita Atlantis, with the PCs as either Theoi tasked to defend the realm from outside aggression/interference or Atlantians trying to investigate/reclaim what they think is part of their lost heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T20:41:12-07:00","id":1340713,"title":"","content":"I have been thinking about this a bit more recently and I just thought of the interesting idea of the players being modern day incarnations of beings from Atlantis, beings whose souls either just managed to wiggle out of the prisons there people are in or who just so happened to have met each other in this particular moment in time. Now they have images of a past world they don't actively remember being in while being chased by other entities who are calling them anathema. The thing is no matter how much they try and avoid it, or maybe break up as a group before the adventure began, things (let us call it fate shall we, hehe) are pushing them towards each other and to something even more glorious - the return to the world the shiny city on the hill that they see in their dreams. <br /> <br /> Just sayin. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T21:07:36-07:00","id":1340718,"title":"","content":"What do you guys think of the idea of the Atlantean &quot;pantheon&quot; actually being the Greek Titans? (By that I mean the second generation of deities between the Protogenoi and the Theoi, just to clarify since &quot;Titan&quot; has a more general meaning in Scion.) Atlantis was a legendary precursor to Greece, and the Titans were the precursors of the Greek gods, so it makes sense. That way Atlantis could have its own pantheon without having to necessarily make any deities up. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T21:11:28-07:00","id":1340719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1340718#post1340718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think of the idea of the Atlantean &amp;quot;pantheon&amp;quot; actually being the Greek Titans? (By that I mean the second generation of deities between the Protogenoi and the Theoi, just to clarify since &amp;quot;Titan&amp;quot; has a more general meaning in Scion.) Atlantis was a legendary precursor to Greece, and the Titans were the precursors of the Greek gods, so it makes sense. That way Atlantis could have its own pantheon without having to necessarily make any deities up. Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do it that way. I obviously wouldn\u2019t use the Teros PSP, Virtues, etc, if so. But that works as the background of Theoi Terra Incognita Atlantis that lies in ruins at the bottom of the sea where Poseidon holds his own court away from Olympus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-11-2019, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T21:42:03-07:00","id":1340727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1340718#post1340718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think of the idea of the Atlantean &quot;pantheon&quot; actually being the Greek Titans? (By that I mean the second generation of deities between the Protogenoi and the Theoi, just to clarify since &quot;Titan&quot; has a more general meaning in Scion.) Atlantis was a legendary precursor to Greece, and the Titans were the precursors of the Greek gods, so it makes sense. That way Atlantis could have its own pantheon without having to necessarily make any deities up. Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean nothing stopping you. I think it sounds dull, especially when the Companion will have a much more interesting-sounding idea. Like... Atlantis doesn't exist. It never existed. It was never intended for people to think it existed. So go fucking nuts with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T22:29:13-07:00","id":1340732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1340727#post1340727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean nothing stopping you. I think it sounds dull, especially when the Companion will have a much more interesting-sounding idea. Like... Atlantis doesn't exist. It never existed. It was never intended for people to think it existed. So go fucking nuts with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it works as a thing to do with Atlantis if you don\u2019t WANT to use Kirbiesque scifi in your myth game, which a lot of people reasonably may not want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T22:36:40-07:00","id":1340733,"title":"","content":"While I love Atlantis in all versions and possibilities the fact that they are going with a unique set of gods is to me a very positive element to what they are doing. But even more it shows the potential of how the game can go in a somewhat different mythic direction. Though I admit to probably looking at the information given about Atlantis in more ways then just for Scion, including finding a way to maybe use it in the Trinity Continuum. hehe <br /> <br /> Of course in that case my (what I think is an) interesting idea for using modern incarnations of ancient Atlantean divinities would have to switch a bit. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T01:17:53-07:00","id":1340749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1340733#post1340733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course in that case my (what I think is an) interesting idea for using modern incarnations of ancient Atlantean divinities would have to switch a bit. hehe</div> </div> </div> </div>I would, if you ran this game idea in Scion, stat them up as Incarnate Scions (So use the PSP, the Motif, all that as though they were Teros) and give them Guides from the Pantheons that gave them. Maybe give them both the Paths of the Teros Pantheon <i>and</i> the Paths of their adopted Pantheon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T07:21:05-07:00","id":1343986,"title":"","content":"Great (and sarcastic ) video summary on the original Atlantis myth, it's modern retellings - and what scientific locations of this land could be! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LXOyw-csJoE\" data-code=\"LXOyw-csJoE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LXOyw-csJoE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Things I got from video I want to put here as subtopics to talk about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Location </b>- Would your Scion Atlantis would be where Plato's myth located in? Other locations pointed by the viedo - like Santorini ( previous Thera Island ) or Britain's Doggerland?<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Plato's Kingdoms</b> - In myth, idea is that Atlantis was really a small 'continent', divided by 10 half human sons of Poseidon-That-Was-Not-Poseidon ( video describe better why it's this ). Interesting would be Terra Incognita divided among 10 Kingdoms, following Theros gods?<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Atlantis Surviving Under Water?</b> Interesting question asked by the modern retelling - could civilization survive under water? Or just being it Terra Incognit solves problem as 'hidden magical land' it is now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T16:39:21-07:00","id":1374653,"title":"","content":"The ancient gods of Rhodes, the Thelcines (I'll look that up tomorrow correct it and post a link) would be an excellent choice to model the gods of Atlantis from. They were smiths and artificers, they lived in the sea banished from land, they warred with the Olympians. They fit being the gods of Atlantis. Heck there are varient ancient myths (disliked in Athens) were the deites of Rhodes raise Poseidon in secret hidden from being eaten by his father.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T18:25:42-07:00","id":1374677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1374653#post1374653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ancient gods of Rhodes, the Thelcines (I'll look that up tomorrow correct it and post a link) would be an excellent choice to model the gods of Atlantis from. They were smiths and artificers, they lived in the sea banished from land, they warred with the Olympians. They fit being the gods of Atlantis. Heck there are varient ancient myths (disliked in Athens) were the deites of Rhodes raise Poseidon in secret hidden from being eaten by his father.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that sounds interesting enough that I'd like to know more. Suggestions for appropriate reading material please?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> For the purposes of your discussion points <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I would lean on the idea that Atlantis was 'destroyed by magic' to the point that it's mundane equivalent was swallowed whole into a Terra Incognita, but I would have access points/touchstones in all three of your listed places. Probably include Antarctica as a reference to it's 1st edition incarnation. Also any place strongly associated with the 'sea people' of the bronze age collapse.</li> <li>That sounds like a neat idea. They could even have been a coalition of kingdoms, uniting only under a high king or emperor when an outside threat is present. More united than Greek city states, but less so than Egypt.</li> <li>Honestly, I would have a few scattered separate survivors; the 'land-dwelling' survivors would all be from wrecked colonial villagers not on the 'mainland'. Said 'mainland' is sunk, taking with it most of their infostructure and experts. There might be merpeople living in those ruins but they would be few in number. Any survivors left would be more like refugees than an active society.</li> </ol><br /> Atlantis went down hard, and bringing it back should be an epic story. Not just convincing them to stop sulking in the corner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 03-13-2020, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T06:15:03-07:00","id":1374747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1374677#post1374677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, that sounds interesting enough that I'd like to know more. Suggestions for appropriate reading material please?<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> For the purposes of your discussion points <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I would lean on the idea that Atlantis was 'destroyed by magic' to the point that it's mundane equivalent was swallowed whole into a Terra Incognita, but I would have access points/touchstones in all three of your listed places. Probably include Antarctica as a reference to it's 1st edition incarnation. Also any place strongly associated with the 'sea people' of the bronze age collapse.</li> <li>That sounds like a neat idea. They could even have been a coalition of kingdoms, uniting only under a high king or emperor when an outside threat is present. More united than Greek city states, but less so than Egypt.</li> <li>Honestly, I would have a few scattered separate survivors; the 'land-dwelling' survivors would all be from wrecked colonial villagers not on the 'mainland'. Said 'mainland' is sunk, taking with it most of their infostructure and experts. There might be merpeople living in those ruins but they would be few in number. Any survivors left would be more like refugees than an active society.</li> </ol><br /> Atlantis went down hard, and bringing it back should be an epic story. Not just convincing them to stop sulking in the corner.</div> </div> </div> </div>The correct spelling is Telchines. There is a Wikipedia article with references and sources. I'd start there. As these are fairly obscure ancient deites unpopular at Athens, expect inconsistent and conflicting stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T12:31:59-07:00","id":1374785,"title":"","content":"After reading the article at <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.theoi.com</a> I think Plato may have based his Atlantis on the Telchines. Atlantis is supposed to be populated by descendents of Poseidon, in some myths the Telchines are descendents of Poseidon, in others Thalassia Titaness of the sea. Skills in magic and smithwork are in both stories. Both the allegory of Atlantis and the myths of the Telchines involve &quot;sins and corruptions&quot; not clearly stated. <br /> <br /> The Telchines seem to have been known to the Athenians, but never integrated into the the standard myths. Thus in some tales they are the children of Poseidon in others his nursemaids and tutors. In some tales they're dogs turned into men in others men cursed by being turned into seals or sea monsters. They supposedly made the sickle that was used to castrate Uranus. It's like Plato took a grab bag and made it a narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T16:30:16-07:00","id":1378398,"title":"","content":"So I don't super follow all the updates of Scion but I was wondering if there have been any news or updates on the Atlantean Pantheon and the companion book that they will be written up in. (Even if I don't actively play Scion I could see myself buying said book if the Atlantis stuff was a nice enough chapter in order to use the material for say a Trinity game or something.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:25:23-07:00","id":1378406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329900-atlantean-pantheon-in-2e?p=1378398#post1378398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't super follow all the updates of Scion but I was wondering if there have been any news or updates on the Atlantean Pantheon and the companion book that they will be written up in. (Even if I don't actively play Scion I could see myself buying said book if the Atlantis stuff was a nice enough chapter in order to use the material for say a Trinity game or something.)</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-teros-of-atlantis-scion-companion/\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a little snippet of the rough direction they're going to take in 2e... And I think upthread I post some snippets I've collected here and there, but I'll repost it here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"